<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_CalibrateGate</defName>
    <driverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Gate.JobDriver_RRCalibrateGate</driverClass>
    <reportString>calibrating the gate</reportString>
    <suspendable>false</suspendable>
    <playerInterruptible>true</playerInterruptible>
    <casualInterruptible>false</casualInterruptible>
    <checkOverrideOnDamage>Always</checkOverrideOnDamage>
  </JobDef>
  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_OperateGate</defName>
    <driverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Gate.JobDriver_RROperateGate</driverClass>
    <reportString>staffing the gate console</reportString>
    <!-- STILL NOT SUSPENDABLE, AND THAT IS NOW A DECISION RATHER THAN THE DEFECT.
         Owner, 2026-10-06: "current a pawn dies at the comms console". The cause was
         this flag PLUS a ToilCompleteMode.Never station PLUS a FailOn that tested no
         need at all — gate, calibration, operator identity, Downed, InMentalState and
         nothing else. So RimWorld could not pull the pawn off and neither could we.

         Handing the decision back to RimWorld by making this suspendable would give
         exactly ONE of the three postures the owner asked for — the mild one — and
         could not express the other two. So the mod keeps the decision and takes the
         duty with it: GateWatch.MustLeave is an absolute floor, asked BEFORE any
         posture, in the FailOn and again every tick. No posture can switch it off, and
         there is deliberately no enum value meaning never leave. -->
    <suspendable>false</suspendable>
    <playerInterruptible>true</playerInterruptible>
    <casualInterruptible>false</casualInterruptible>
    <checkOverrideOnDamage>Always</checkOverrideOnDamage>
  </JobDef>
  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_ReconditionGate</defName>
    <driverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Gate.JobDriver_RRReconditionGate</driverClass>
    <reportString>monitoring and adjusting the gate assembly</reportString>
    <suspendable>false</suspendable>
    <playerInterruptible>true</playerInterruptible>
    <casualInterruptible>false</casualInterruptible>
    <checkOverrideOnDamage>Always</checkOverrideOnDamage>
  </JobDef>

  <!-- Writing one piece of the company's paperwork at a records desk.

       SUSPENDABLE AND CASUALLY INTERRUPTIBLE, which is the opposite of RR_OperateGate above, and
       the contrast is the decision. A gate window is a scarce thing somebody might reasonably want
       held through discomfort, which is why that job keeps the decision and takes the duty with it.
       A report is not scarce and nothing is waiting on it, so RimWorld gets to pull the pawn off
       for anything it likes.

       The driver still asks GateWatch.MustLeave in its FailOn and again every tick. That is not
       belt-and-braces: a suspendable job can still be entered by a pawn who is already starving,
       and the floor exists so a pawn never begins work it should not. -->
  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_WriteUp</defName>
    <driverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Company.JobDriver_RRWriteUp</driverClass>
    <reportString>writing up company paperwork at TargetA.</reportString>
    <suspendable>true</suspendable>
    <casualInterruptible>true</casualInterruptible>
    <allowOpportunisticPrefix>false</allowOpportunisticPrefix>
  </JobDef>

  <!-- Writing one room into the record book while exploring.

       Owner, 2026-10-06: "survey should go hand in hand with the auto explore and person has task to
       write in journal when exploring each room for like 20 seconds". The driver's RoomSurveyTicks is
       1200, which is twenty seconds at normal speed.

       Suspendable and casually interruptible, like the records desk and unlike RR_OperateGate: a
       survey is not a scarce window anybody is holding, and a pawn who needs to eat should eat. The
       explore toggle stays on, so they resume the room when they come back. -->
  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_ExploreRoom</defName>
    <driverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Generation.JobDriver_RRExploreRoom</driverClass>
    <reportString>writing up this room.</reportString>
    <suspendable>true</suspendable>
    <casualInterruptible>true</casualInterruptible>
    <allowOpportunisticPrefix>false</allowOpportunisticPrefix>
  </JobDef>
</Defs>
